Scope

This licence covers the code of "Predicting the Sky": every .js and .css
file, the HTML markup of the pages, and everything under tools/. The text,
figures, exercises and plates of the pages are licensed separately, under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0: see LICENSE-CONTENT.md.

Third-party material

The following keep their own licences and are not covered by this one:

- KaTeX (https://katex.org), loaded from cdnjs to typeset the equations:
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Khan Academy and other contributors.
- The fonts Cormorant Garamond, Cormorant SC (Copyright 2015 the Cormorant
  Project Authors) and Spectral (Copyright 2017 The Spectral Project
  Authors), loaded from Google Fonts: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
- astronomy-engine (https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy), a
  development-only dependency used to cross-check the reference sky, not
  shipped with the site: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019-2023 Don Cross
  (version 2.1.19).
- The photos: each keeps the licence recorded in the images/CREDITS.md file
  of its page and in its caption.
- The data and methods of others (SIMBAD, E. M. Standish's elements from
  JPL, Meeus' Astronomical Algorithms, the precession of Vondrák, Capitaine
  and Wallace), as credited in the Sources section of each page.
